{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1865 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8db0d3428194c7b6f0be7f070c0775bb8f0fffaf939e26e953bab6fa0cc98473" :edb/db-before-t 1864 :edb/db-after-t 1865 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535177 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:45:34.701Z" 13194139535177 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335664 13194139535177 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335669 13194139535177 true] [17592186157784 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535177 true] [17592186157784 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056541/assets/75df54dd30da590814e89153396ac7cf8a713fc9a6e04d14786780147ba57cfe.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535177 true] [17592186157784 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2837/Source/Images/q-84467.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)$, generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535177 false] [17592186157784 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(5,-1),$ and passes through the point $(17,11).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(5,-1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-5=p{t}^{2},\\,y+1=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(17,11),$ we can substitute $x=17$ and $y=11$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12=p{t}^{2} \\\\ 12=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =2pt \\\\ 6 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{6}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =p{(\\frac{6}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 12 & =p\\cdot \\frac{36}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{36}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-5=(3){t}^{2},\\,y+1=2(3)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-5=3{t}^{2},\\,y+1=6t.\n$$" 13194139535177 true] [17592186292089 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056541/assets/6cd9c6a97d450761c01a9adb723985acbf4e5dc91e9877d7bd46c95db66d8c30.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535177 true] [17592186292089 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/assets/6cd9c6a97d450761c01a9adb723985acbf4e5dc91e9877d7bd46c95db66d8c30.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139535177 false] [17592186335664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335665 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335667 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1089 "q-321592" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx+2=5t,\\,y-2={t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1113 #uuid "4b38783e-1aa6-5722-8348-08e33fa245db" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335664 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\frac{x+2}{5},\\,{t}^{2}=y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{x+2}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=y-2$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25} & =y-2 \\\\ {(x+2)}^{2} & =25(y-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335666 13194139535177 true] [17592186335665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535177 true] [17592186335665 1041 "field-1" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335666 13194139535177 true] [17592186335665 1110 #uuid "65ae4835-b693-58ed-ba98-152de30a9ad6" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335666 1034 "2" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335666 1111 #uuid "29acce41-c002-5d4b-8e0c-899e03b85800" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335668 13194139535177 true] [17592186335667 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535177 true] [17592186335667 1041 "field-2" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335667 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335668 13194139535177 true] [17592186335667 1110 #uuid "444f7d45-5653-53bd-904d-da9149a5e623" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335668 1034 "25(y-2)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335668 1111 #uuid "52a2a18b-c37c-5810-9b54-40770c679e30" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335670 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1089 "q-84855" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-3=-6t,\\,y-1=-3{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1113 #uuid "47d76f1d-d242-5bf6-8664-6b58d2510ca1" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335669 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x-3}{6},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x-3}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-1}{3}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36} & =-\\frac{y-1}{3} \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =36\\cdot (-\\frac{y-1}{3}) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =-12(y-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335671 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335672 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335673 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335674 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335675 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1041 "selection" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335672 13194139535177 true] [17592186335670 1110 #uuid "a9acdab2-5744-579e-baad-36edcbaf391e" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335671 1034 "(x+3)^{2}=12(y+1)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335671 1111 #uuid "e78fc381-1d46-548b-81d4-3c22b2a741b1" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335672 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=-12(y-1)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335672 1111 #uuid "decc5de0-73b9-5ba6-813f-b8ee87a392e3" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335673 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=-6(y-1)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335673 1111 #uuid "4dbffa8e-abed-5a51-a13a-d1d32514a346" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335674 1034 "(x-3)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(y-1)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535177 true] [17592186335674 1111 #uuid "01ca4d8d-f5bd-5d8c-bcd6-1a21ad35a1b8" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335675 1034 "(x+3)^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(y+1)" 13194139535177 true] [17592186335675 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604